dsh-session-hub README · Requirements：**Last verified 2026-08-14**: remote side — local Windows + Node v24.9.0 against remote OpenCloudOS 9.4 +
Node v24.9.0 over an SSH tunnel: cross-machine dialogue, approval answering and the live stream end to end;
import side — 615 local sessions parsed (Codex 523 / Claude Code 67 / opencode 25) into 21 workspaces,
read-only → real-session promotion verified.

> The config format, route table and `/hub/events` frame protocol may still change within a minor version.

dsh-session-hub README · Importing sessions from other tools：- Tools you have not clicked **Import** for are never read — not a byte;
- Tick **Auto**: a 60-second periodic scan plus incremental re-parsing on import picks up newly written log
  rows; unticked, updates only when you click refresh;
- Imported sessions are read-only in the tree, with **tool calls rendered as real cards** (arguments, results,
  error flags) in source-log order. Call ids, arguments and outputs all come from the original records —
  nothing is synthesized;
- **Remove**: pulls that tool's sessions out of the tree, no effect on other tools, original logs untouched;
- Imported sessions are read-only; sending a message to one automatically promotes it to a real DSH session
  (user/assistant turns and tool calls preserved, the read-only original hidden).

dsh-session-hub README · What it accesses：**SSH keys**: tunnel entries read the private key at the path you provide (only to establish that tunnel);
key material is never persisted, never sent anywhere, never written into the plugin config — the config
stores the path only. Left empty, the ssh agent is used and the plugin never touches key material.
